  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced institutional and national capacities for  inclusive, gender-responsive, and sustainable social protection strategies, policies, and legal frameworks, ensuring sound governance and adequate financing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India&#x2019;s social security system is complex with the combination of central, state and occupational welfare boards&#x2019; schemes. Certain autonomy is given to each state and therefore a review of social security system has to be conducted at the state level while the review results of central schemes need to be taken into account. ILO&#x2019;s technical assistance will be aligned to support the priorities of the constituents. The key focus of the CPO will be: ILO-ESIC project on improving health sector in India,  extension of social protection to gig and platform workers; providing technical assistance to the governement for addressing Social protection data deficiency that would reflect improvement in coverage of social protection in India;</narrative>
  </description>
